            <div xml:id="d585">

                <pb facs="0716" n="572" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg572"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.003/106: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-05-31T15:00:00+08:00">May 31, 1929—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 31—7:48 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>435. Following from the Minister at Nanking:</p>
                <p>May 30, 9 p.m. Today the Japanese Minister informed several of his colleagues,
                    myself included, that he had received a confidential intimation from a “fairly
                    authoritative source” in the Chinese Government <pb facs="0717" n="573"
                        xml:id="pg573"/> of its intention to declare the abolition next January 1 of
                    all extraterritorial rights. The Belgian Minister said he, too, had received a
                    somewhat less definite intimation from the Minister for Foreign Affairs to the
                    same effect.</p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
